  <!-- ============ FEATURES ============ -->
  <section id="features" aria-labelledby="features-h">
    <h2 id="features-h">Features</h2>
    <ul class="features">
      <li><b>Three reverb engines</b><span>Dark FDN 1 for sub-weight, Dark FDN 2 for a bright, moving wash, and the plate from Mutable Instruments' Rings.</span></li>
      <li><b>Drive</b><span>Tube, Iron or Transistor saturation on the switch, from clean to obliterated. Each output is driven on its own, so the sub stays a sub.</span></li>
      <li><b>Split</b><span>Set the cutoff between rumble and texture. Everything below it goes to the rumble output, everything above to the texture output.</span></li>
      <li><b>Predelay and Diffusion</b><span>Predelay moves the swell off the kick, up to 500 ms. Diffusion spreads the early reflections, from distinct doubles of the kick to a smooth thickening.</span></li>
      <li><b>Built-in sidechain</b><span>Every kick ducks the rumble out of its way. Release sets how fast it swells back; Texture duck sets how much the texture follows.</span></li>
      <li><b>Mix In</b><span>Noise for grit, or any other source. Mix it in with the kick at the start of the chain, or at the output stage.</span></li>
      <li><b>Hot outputs</b><span>Both outputs run near full level with a soft clipper as a safety net. Set the level at your mixer.</span></li>
      <li><b>Seven CV inputs</b><span>One per knob.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ LISTEN ============ -->
  <section id="listen" aria-labelledby="listen-h">
    <h2 id="listen-h">Listen</h2>
